## Story Description
Four targeted improvements to the Overview page: (1) replace the weakest KPI (Invoice Count) with Tail Spend %, which is a core procurement diagnostic; (2) wire the supplier bar chart so clicking a supplier name navigates to the Supplier page; (3) wire the category treemap so clicking a category navigates to the Category page; (4) add a concentration stat line below the supplier chart title; (5) add a data freshness date below the page title so users always know what period they are analysing.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/OverviewPage.tsx
- Add import: import { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom'
- Add const navigate = useNavigate() inside the component
- Replace the Invoice Count KpiCard with: <KpiCard label='Tail Spend' value={overview?.tail_spend_pct ?? 0} valueType='pct' accentColor={overview?.tail_spend_pct != null && overview.tail_spend_pct > 30 ? 'risk' : overview?.tail_spend_pct != null && overview.tail_spend_pct > 15 ? 'amber' : 'green'} benchmarkLabel='% of spend in tail suppliers' />
- Wire the supplier SpendBarChart: add prop onBarClick={(label) => navigate(`/engagements/${engagementId}/supplier`)} and clickHint={true}. This navigates to the supplier page; no pre-filtering needed.
- Wire the SpendTreemap: add prop onCellClick={(name) => navigate(`/engagements/${engagementId}/category`)}
- Add concentration stat: compute top10Spend = supplierData.slice(0, 10).reduce((s, r) => s + (r.total_spend ?? 0), 0). Compute allSpend = supplierData.reduce((s, r) => s + (r.total_spend ?? 0), 0). In the supplier chart container, change the title from the existing plain h3 to a div with flex justify-between: left side is the 'Top 10 Suppliers' section-header, right side is a span className='text-xs text-muted-foreground' showing: allSpend > 0 ? `Top 10 = ${((top10Spend/allSpend)*100).toFixed(1)}% of total spend` : ''
- Add date context: below the h1 'Spend Overview' heading, add: {overview?.data_freshness && <p className='text-sm text-muted-foreground -mt-4'>{formatDate(overview.data_freshness)}</p>}. Import formatDate from @/lib/formatters.
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — zero TypeScript errors

