## Story Description
Add a selectedLabel prop to SpendBarChart so the currently-selected bar can be visually distinguished from others. When a bar is selected, it renders at full opacity with a 2px white stroke border; other bars render at 0.65 opacity. This is needed by the Category page to confirm which L1 bar is active.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/components/charts/SpendBarChart.tsx
- Add optional prop selectedLabel?: string to the SpendBarChartProps interface and destructure it in the function signature (default undefined)
- Inside the Bar component's Cell rendering: when colors is provided or selectedLabel is provided, render Cell components for every bar. For each bar: if selectedLabel is set and entry.name === selectedLabel, render <Cell key={...} fill={colors?.[index] ?? color} opacity={1} stroke='#ffffff' strokeWidth={2} />. If selectedLabel is set and entry.name !== selectedLabel, render <Cell key={...} fill={colors?.[index] ?? color} opacity={0.55} />. If selectedLabel is not set and colors is provided, render <Cell key={...} fill={colors[index] ?? color} />.
- When neither colors nor selectedLabel is provided, the Bar renders with its single fill prop as before (no Cell children) — ensure this case still works
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — zero TypeScript errors

